WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:09.564
"Fecal Transplants for Aging
and Weight Loss"

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.520
Hippocrates said,
All diseases begin in the gut.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.340
Previously, I've talked
about fecal transplants,

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.880
transferring the stool of healthy
people into the colons of patients

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.300
suffering from inflammatory bowel
disease, multiple sclerosis,

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.260
even psychiatric problems
like depression, bipolar disorder,

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.280
and alcoholism to repopulate
their gut with good bacteria

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.866
in hopes of improving
their conditions.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.400
What about fecal
transplants for aging?

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.771
Might the fountain of youth
be a fountain of poop?

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.420
If you give mice
with accelerated aging

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.140
a fecal transplant from healthy
mice, they perk up and live longer,

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.000
but what about
human poop?

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.120
We don’t yet have human-
to-human aging data,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.400
but we do have mice
transplanted

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.320
with fecal matter
from a centenarian.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.360
Mice fed poop from a 101-year-old
versus poop from a 70-year-old.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.240
Lipofuscin is an age pigment

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.460
that’s widely used
as a biomarker for aging,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.100
and lipofuscin accumulated
significantly less

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:16.080
in the brain tissue of centenarian
poop-fed mice raising the possibility

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.860
that we will one day be using
centenarian fecal matter

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:23.800
for anti-aging purposes
and to promote healthy aging.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.280
Why bathe in the
blood of virgins

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.273
when you can dine on
the dung of the venerable?

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.860
To be continued,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.200
once human-to-human
data are published.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.980
Poop you may want to avoid
is from overweight stool donors,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.520
given this case report about weight
gain after a fecal transplant.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.640
A 32-year-old woman
“had always been of normal weight”

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.820
until...she received a fecal
transplant from a healthy

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.100
but overweight
donor – her daughter.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.100
After the transplant
she became obese,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.080
gaining more
than 40 pounds.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.380
“She said she felt like there
was a switch inside her body,”

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.180
her gastroenterologist reported.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.860
“No matter how much
she ate or exercised,

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.540
she couldn’t take
the weight off.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.640
She’s very frustrated.”

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.320
The same thing
happens in mice.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.020
Giving mice fecal pellets
from an obese mouse

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:12.275
resulted in nearly a doubling
in fat mass

00:02:12.275 --> 00:02:13.981
compared to lean mouse pellets

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.740
despite eating
significantly fewer calories.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:22.860
This proves gut flora can play
a pivotal role in obesity…in mice.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.850
What about in people?

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:27.000
Researchers decided
to study pairs

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.520
of human twins
“discordant” for obesity,

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.980
meaning one twin was fat,
the other skinny.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.400
What would happen if you
switched their microbiomes?

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.860
The siblings may
have been squeamish;

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.380
so, the researchers
reverted to mice again.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.040
Mice fed stool from the obese
twin rapidly swelled in size

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.620
but not those fed
from the lean twin,

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.701
despite comparable
calorie intakes.

00:02:49.887 --> 00:02:53.400
Cohousing the mice together
prevented the weight gain;

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.580
however, the lean-type
bacteria jumped over to rescue

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.280
the mouse fed stool
from the obese twin, but—

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.540
and here’s the critical point—

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.840
only in the context
of a healthier diet.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.220
The microbial cure only
worked when the mice were fed

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.220
low saturated fat, high-fiber
diets, which makes sense

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:15.120
since the lean-type bacteria
appeared to be fiber feeders.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.460
“Together,” the researchers
concluded,

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.180
“these results…illustrate how
a diet high in saturated fats

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.820
and low in fruits and vegetables
can select against

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:27.780
human gut bacteria…
associated with leanness.”

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.340
The results of the twin study

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:30.960
suggest that the role
of our gut flora

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.180
in obesity is just to help take

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.760
fuller advantage
of a more healthful diet.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.700
So, if the twins had actually
swapped their stool,

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.060
the obese twin might have only
lost weight if they combined

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:45.120
the microbial makeover
with healthier eating

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.820
to aid the colonization
of the better bugs.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.640
With the new bacteria
on board, though,

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.700
the healthier diet could have
resulted in more weight loss,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.020
even eating the same
number of calories.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:01.040
But you don’t really know...
until you put it to the test.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.540
There had been previous
published attempts,

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.760
randomized double-blind
placebo-controlled trials

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.440
showing no weight
loss benefit

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.840
to getting lean donor
fecal transplants,

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.140
but they kept people
on the same crappy diets

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.000
that led to obesity
in the first place.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.760
Who cares if you keep
putting slimming,

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.680
fiber-feeding bacteria
into your gut,

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.300
if you don’t give them
any fiber to eat?

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.100
They’ll just starve
and die right off.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.660
So, maybe you have to do both,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.620
pairing gut bacteria modulation
with a dietary intervention.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.340
But, if you do a plant-based
diet along with a transplant

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.540
and they lose
a bunch of weight,

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:36.840
how do you know if the transplant
had anything to do with it?

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.660
Which brings us to this study,

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.600
What they did is put people
on a healthy plant-based diet

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:44.820
supplemented with green tea
and green smoothies

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.980
until...they lost
about 20 pounds

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.560
over 6 months and grabbed
a fecal sample.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.560
Then, they were randomized
to spend the rest of the year

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.500
constantly seeding their gut
with the healthy microbiome

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.640
they had achieved at maximal
weight loss or to placebo capsules.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:04.020
The question was once they go
back to their regular diets,

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:07.200
would those getting the constant
infusion of their own skinny poop

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.020
help them keep the weight off? Yes.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:13.080
They found that participants
who lost weight on a healthy diet

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.080
and were then fed capsules
containing fecal matter collected

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.020
during the diet period for months
after the maximal weight loss,

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:22.980
regained less weight than
participants given placebo capsules.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:25.380
So, the plant-based diet
appeared to produce

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:29.280
the optimal fecal microbiome
for preventing weight regain.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:33.120
But rather than eating
your own plant-based poo,

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.664
why not just stick
with the plant-based diet.

